Corporate Social Responsibility (CSR) & Sustainability:
MNEs should support human rights, environmental protection, and fair trade practices.
Transparency in business operations, supply chains, and labor policies is required.
The MNE Declaration aligns multinational businesses with international labor standards, ensuring ethical corporate behavior and sustainable economic growth.', 'ILO', 'climate', 'in_force', '2017-01-01'::date, 'ITCILO', 'https://training.itcilo.org/delta/MNE/downloads/MNE-Employers.pdf', ARRAY['guidance_frameworks', 'ilo', 'other sustainability policy', 'sdg10', 'sdg8', 'sdg7', 'sdg16', 'sdg12', 'sdg15', 'voluntary']::text[]) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO regulations (id, title, formal_title, summary, description, full_description, region, category, status, effective_date, source_name, source_url, tags) VALUES ('d3ffe48c-f9d5-5540-ba70-0b2dca81103e', 'ILO Tripartite Declaration of Principles Concerning Multinational Enterprises', 'Tripartite Declaration of Principles Concerning Multinational Enterprises and Social Policy, 2001', 'The principles laid down in this universal instrument offer guidelines to MNEs, governments, and employers’ and workers’ organizations in such areas as employment, training, conditions of work and life, and industrial relations. Its provisions are reinforced by certain international labour Conventions and Recommendations which the social partners are urged to bear in mind and apply, to the greatest extent possible. The adoption of the ILO Declaration on Fundamental Principles and Rights at Work and its Follow-up in 1998 highlighted the importance of the fundamental Conventions in realizing the objectives of the ILO, and consequently, the MNE Declaration takes into account the objectives of the 1998 Declaration.', 'The principles laid down in this universal instrument offer guidelines to MNEs, governments, and employers’ and workers’ organizations in such areas as employment, training, conditions of work and life, and industrial relations. Its provisions are reinforced by certain international labour Conventions and Recommendations which the social partners are urged to bear in mind and apply, to the greatest extent possible. The adoption of the ILO Declaration on Fundamental Principles and Rights at Work and its Follow-up in 1998 highlighted the importance of the fundamental Conventions in realizing the objectives of the ILO, and consequently, the MNE Declaration takes into account the objectives of the 1998 Declaration.', 'The principles laid down in this universal instrument offer guidelines to MNEs, governments, and employers’ and workers’ organizations in such areas as employment, training, conditions of work and life, and industrial relations. Its provisions are reinforced by certain international labour Conventions and Recommendations which the social partners are urged to bear in mind and apply, to the greatest extent possible. The adoption of the ILO Declaration on Fundamental Principles and Rights at Work and its Follow-up in 1998 highlighted the importance of the fundamental Conventions in realizing the objectives of the ILO, and consequently, the MNE Declaration takes into account the objectives of the 1998 Declaration.', 'ILO', 'climate', 'in_force', '2001-01-01'::date, 'ITCILO', 'https://training.itcilo.org/delta/MNE/downloads/MNE-Employers.pdf', ARRAY['sdg4', 'guidance_frameworks', 'ilo', 'other sustainability policy', 'sdg8', 'voluntary']::text[]) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;
